{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F1, frames and context, addresses finite actors' declaration, sizing, binding, activation, relations, coverage audit and revision of bounded frames. Its instance premises are: a workspace exceeds one actor's competence, context, tools and access; evaluations are declared questions about a governed outcome; actors and frames may overlap; workspace topology and capabilities change between activations; and actors may read owning sources or copied, projected or compressed surfaces. These are conditions of the governed work, not commitments or consequences of finite capacity alone. P0's cited actor-change premise permits reacquisition of declared sources, not private memory; its cited open-world premise leaves the world open.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":147,
          "quote":"They are conditions of the work this family governs, not\ncommitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":143
        }
      ],
      "key":"frames_context_family",
      "label":"Frames and context family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations required by one evaluation family. Its engagement unit is one activated bounded context, distinct from semantic irreducibility, runtime carriers and the functions over frames. The member's bounded-context identity is urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":157,
          "quote":"a reference frame is a finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations one evaluation family requires.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":157
        }
      ],
      "key":"reference_frame",
      "label":"Reference frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The declared questions or predicates supported by a frame, at its declared coordinates, against which its sufficiency is testable.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":284,
          "quote":"Every frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-001%20Evaluation%20relativity",
          "start_line":283
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_family",
      "label":"Evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The selected actor's declared capability boundary, including competence, context capacity, tools and access. Context fit and adequate attention during actual use are distinct questions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":290,
          "quote":"An activated frame contains a finite attention surface that fits the\nselected actor's declared capability envelope.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-002%20Finite%20attention",
          "start_line":289
        }
      ],
      "key":"actor_capability_envelope",
      "label":"Actor capability envelope"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The laws applicable to every declared or activated frame; their named objects are defined in FOUNDATIONS §2.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":279,
          "quote":"Every frame, declared or activated, obeys the following. The objects named\nare defined in FOUNDATIONS §2.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws",
          "start_line":278
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_laws",
      "label":"Frame laws"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A project selection of frames declared by human authority for a governed workspace and outcome. It need not be a partition, tree, stack, exhaustive ontology or uniquely minimal set.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":480,
          "quote":"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated\ndevelopment practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the governed\noutcome's risk and knowledge of the available agents and other actors. The\ndeclaration need not reconstruct the set from the workspace bottom up",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration",
          "start_line":476
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_set",
      "label":"Project frame set"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "One closed result returned by a performed frame evaluation in its declared algebra, with exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence scope. No evaluation result exists for an evaluation not performed.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":401,
          "quote":"Every performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\ninto it under that section.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results",
          "start_line":398
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_result",
      "label":"Closed frame result"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The source's imported result domain has five core values: satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis. FOUNDATIONS §4 owns their meanings, refinement and combination rules; REFERENCE_FRAME applies them without redefining them.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":403,
          "quote":"That section owns the five core values\n(`satisfied`, `falsified`, `indeterminate`, `out_of_frame` and\n`invalid_basis`)",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results",
          "start_line":401
        }
      ],
      "key":"core_result_domain",
      "label":"Imported core result algebra"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Seven relations distinct from frames: declare(human_authority, workspace, outcome, practices, capabilities) → frame_set; activate(frame, evaluation, subject, basis, actor) → activated_frame or activation_refusal; evaluate(activated_frame, admissible_evidence) → result with evidence and residuals; conjoin(decision_rule, frame_results) → decision, conflict or indeterminate; translate(source_frame, target_frame, value_or_evidence, mapping) → translated_value, declared_loss or refusal; audit_coverage(workspace, outcome, evaluation_inventory, frame_set) → coverage_ledger; revise(frame_set, new_evidence, failures, capability_change, topology_change) → proposed_frame_set_delta. Later clauses supplement the displayed signatures with direct out_of_frame and invalid_basis outcomes.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":552,
          "quote":"revise(frame_set, new_evidence, failures, capability_change, topology_change)\n  -> proposed_frame_set_delta",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions",
          "start_line":551
        },
        {
          "end_line":530,
          "quote":"The frame and the functions over it remain distinct. An application may\nrealise the following relations in any conforming form; the signatures\ndescribe relations, not callable software interfaces",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions",
          "start_line":527
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_method_functions",
      "label":"Method functions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Exchange of information between frames or actors activated on them. Configuration assigns information exchanges as well as responsibilities; exchange alone is neither an authority grant nor a decomposition or evaluation dependency.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":366,
          "quote":"Communication is the exchange of\ninformation between frames, or between the actors activated on them.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-009%20No%20assumed%20hierarchy",
          "start_line":364
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_communication",
      "label":"Frame communication"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A semantic unit whose irreducibility is separate from a frame's engagement atomicity. Several semantic atoms may occur in one frame, and one semantic atom may participate in several frames.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":465,
          "quote":"Semantic irreducibility is a\nseparate question: one frame may contain several semantic atoms, and one\nsemantic atom may take part in several frames",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FEngagement%20atom%20and%20semantic%20atom",
          "start_line":463
        }
      ],
      "key":"semantic_atom",
      "label":"Semantic atom"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The evaluation requires the relation."],
      "definition": "Four distinct ways frames act together: independently activated co-evaluation, result conjunction, evidence or coordinate translation, and material composition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":614,
          "quote":"Frames act together through four distinct relations, and only where the\nevaluation requires one",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction",
          "start_line":613
        }
      ],
      "key":"frames_in_conjunction",
      "label":"Frames acting together"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Separate activations through which several frames may evaluate the same subject and return closed results, serving assurance independence, different evidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives. Structural disjointness, procedural evaluation independence and claim-relative assurance independence remain different relations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":623,
          "quote":"Several frames may evaluate the same subject through separate activations\nand return closed results. They may overlap in subject, manifold or\nevidence sources; neither evaluation consumes or influences the other's\nunclosed working result. This serves assurance independence, different\nevidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FIndependently%20activated%20co-evaluation",
          "start_line":618
        },
        {
          "end_line":167,
          "quote":"frame disjointness (structural), evaluation independence (procedural) and assurance independence (claim-relative) are three relations",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":167
        }
      ],
      "key":"independent_co_evaluation",
      "label":"Independently activated co-evaluation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A declared decision rule consuming closed results of several frames over the imported core values. FOUNDATIONS §4 owns the rule's required declaration and computation; this member defines no separate conjunction.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":632,
          "quote":"A declared decision rule consumes the closed results of several frames.\nThe rule, what it must state, and the conjunction it computes are\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results](FOUNDATIONS.md#conjunction-of-results),\nover the core values of [FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results);\nthis member defines no conjunction of its own.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FResult%20conjunction",
          "start_line":627
        }
      ],
      "key":"result_conjunction",
      "label":"Result conjunction"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another."],
      "definition": "A declared transport of evidence or values between frames, identifying source and target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":639,
          "quote":"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another. The\ntranslation declares source and target coordinates, preserved meaning,\naccepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation",
          "start_line":636
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_translation",
      "label":"Evidence or coordinate translation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The evaluation requires composition."],
      "definition": "Several frame-governed operations forming one material execution or reasoning relation declared by the owning application.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":654,
          "quote":"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning\nrelation. The owning application declares the composition, the shared\ninvariants, the effect or decision order where material, closure, failure,\nand the conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FMaterial%20composition",
          "start_line":651
        }
      ],
      "key":"material_composition",
      "label":"Material composition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Ten possible frame relations: disjoint shares no material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency for declared evaluations; overlapping shares some material variables, evidence or entities; complementary has distinct evaluations jointly informing one decision; alternative permits different frames to evaluate one claim under declared capability or evidence conditions; refinement resolves a material distinction aggregated in another; restriction evaluates a lawful subset of another's domain; translated moves values or evidence through a declared coordinate map; temporally successive evaluates a changed basis in a later frame; composed forms one governed evaluation or action from several frame relations; governing and subordinate inherits declared constraints where a real authority or decomposition relation exists.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":678,
          "quote":"- governing and subordinate: one frame inherits declared constraints from\n  another where a real authority or decomposition relation exists.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations",
          "start_line":677
        },
        {
          "end_line":664,
          "quote":"- disjoint: no material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency\n  is shared for the declared evaluations;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations",
          "start_line":663
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_relation_categories",
      "label":"Frame relation categories"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The document's workspace-coverage subject, elaborated through coverage basis, inventory, dimensions, ledger, interaction, authority, failure, separately activated checks and operational full coverage.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":684,
          "quote":"## 8. Workspace coverage",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage",
          "start_line":684
        }
      ],
      "key":"workspace_coverage",
      "label":"Workspace coverage"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): workspace, governed outcome, exact basis, known evaluation inventory, declared frame set and time or immutable checkpoint of the claim.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":691,
          "quote":"Coverage is evaluated against the tuple Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): the\nworkspace W, the governed outcome G, the exact basis B, the known\nevaluation inventory E, the declared frame set S and the time or immutable\ncheckpoint T of the claim.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20basis",
          "start_line":688
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_tuple",
      "label":"Coverage basis tuple"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The known material evaluations derived by the coverage evaluator from all material available sources, recording provenance and materiality.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":700,
          "quote":"The coverage evaluator derives the known evaluation inventory from every\nmaterial available source",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FEvaluation%20inventory",
          "start_line":699
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_inventory",
      "label":"Evaluation inventory"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Cross-cutting audit lenses, typically outcome and capability; identity and authority; lifecycle and temporal behaviour; topology and interaction seams; transport and representation; evidence and proof; change, failure, recovery and rollback; historical regression; actor capability and context fit. These become frames only when separately instantiated as bounded evaluation families.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":723,
          "quote":"These are lenses (FOUNDATIONS §2): they become frames only when separately\ninstantiated as bounded evaluation families",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20dimensions",
          "start_line":722
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_dimensions",
      "label":"Coverage dimensions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Per-evaluation coverage records whose baseline statuses are covered, separately_covered, conditionally_covered, conflicted, uncovered, unknown and excluded_by_authority. Statuses answer whether the row's coverage obligation is met on the declared tuple by capable conflict-free coverage or a cited governing exclusion.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":748,
          "quote":"The baseline coverage statuses are `covered`, `separately_covered`,\n`conditionally_covered`, `conflicted`, `uncovered`, `unknown` and\n`excluded_by_authority`.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger",
          "start_line":746
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_ledger",
      "label":"Coverage ledger"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The document's discovery-and-revision subject, comprising missing-frame signals, ordered diagnosis and permitted revision actions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":861,
          "quote":"## 10. Discovery and revision",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision",
          "start_line":861
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_discovery_revision",
      "label":"Discovery and revision"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The supplied context for one activated frame or one declared active frame configuration, enabling a fresh competent actor to reconstruct its evaluation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":970,
          "quote":"An actor receives one activated frame or one declared active frame\nconfiguration, never an implied demand to reconstruct the complete\nworkspace from ambient context",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet",
          "start_line":967
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_packet",
      "label":"Activation packet"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Carrier-neutral content sufficient to bind one declared frame for one evaluation: stable activation identity; declaration identity and revision; exact evaluation and closed algebra; exact subject or candidate; workspace, authority, dependency, configuration and time basis; material relations and invariants; exact source and semantic references; exclusions and prohibited assumptions; actor and capability envelope; semantic and evaluation authority; operation authority, subject and territory where material; decision, acceptance and publication authority; admissible evidence and acquisition route; used dependency, overlap, input, conjunction or translation relations; expected consumer and return relation; invalidation, stop, residual, re-entry and reconfiguration conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":997,
          "quote":"The following carrier-neutral content is sufficient to bind one declared\nframe for one evaluation. It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding",
          "start_line":994
        }
      ],
      "key":"minimal_activation_binding",
      "label":"Minimal activation binding template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Three carrier-neutral shapes stating the least content for declaring a frame, frame set and evaluation result; each is sufficient in Markdown or another consumer-selected carrier.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1076,
          "quote":"The three carrier-neutral shapes below are the least content that declares\na frame, a frame set and an evaluation result. Each is sufficient as\nwritten in Markdown or any other consumer-selected carrier",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations",
          "start_line":1073
        }
      ],
      "key":"minimal_declaration_shapes",
      "label":"Minimal declarations"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Frame template content: stable local identity; evaluation questions, predicates and closed algebra; workspace boundary, exact identity and version/time/topology coordinates; material entities, variables, relations, states and interactions; coordinates and equality; governing invariants; frame-set, semantic, evaluation, operation where material and decision authority; admissible evidence, provenance and exclusions; competence, context, access, tools, evaluation/assurance independence and configuration; irrelevant material, prohibited assumptions and out-of-frame conditions; optional input, output, overlap, conjunction and translation relations actually used; invalidation and recharting changes; representative qualification cases, counterexamples and known residuals.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1089,
          "quote":"# Frame: <stable local identity>\n\n## Evaluation Family\n<questions, predicates, and closed result algebra>\n\n## Subject And Basis\n<workspace boundary, exact identity, version/time/topology coordinates>",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame%20declaration",
          "start_line":1083
        }
      ],
      "key":"minimal_frame_declaration",
      "label":"Minimal frame declaration template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Frame-set template content: stable local identity; workspace, outcome, basis and time; human declaration and acceptance authority; known material evaluations with provenance; selected frame identities, revisions and envelopes; evaluation-to-capable-frame rationale; intentional separately activated checks, assurance-independence conditions or alternative capability fit; only required conjunction and translation relations; uncovered, unknown, conditional or excluded evaluations; revision triggers from history, topology, capability, evidence or outcome changes.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1136,
