      "key":"finite_attention_and_measurement",
      "statement":"The finite attention surface must fit the selected actor's declared envelope; dependence on undeclared ambient memory, conversation history or effectively global context makes it unreconstructable for that actor. When context capacity is declared, measure selected context before reading, state the boundary, record size, capacity and comparison, and mark outside context unmeasured. Measurement establishes fit only within that boundary, not adequate attention, a resource budget or a universal gate. ACTIVATION §2 owns measurement applicability; EVALUATION §7 uses actual-use evidence for adequate attention. Capacity and bytes/tokens belong to the envelope; measurement boundary and time, spend and other limits belong to the selected execution binding.",
